<title>USA: Columbus McKinnon Corp Q3 net falls.</title>
<headline>Columbus McKinnon Corp Q3 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO, N.Y. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>THREE MONTHS ENDED	   29-Dec-96  31-Dec-95  31-Dec-95</p>
<p>					     Actual  Actual  Pro Forma*</p>
<p> Net sales				  $103,393 $53,408 $104,312</p>
<p> Gross profit				 30,104  15,115   29,981</p>
<p>Net income before loss on</p>
<p>     debt extinguishment		$3,219    $2,756  $1,815</p>
<p>    Net EPS before loss		  $0.25     $0.39    0.14</p>
<p>    Wgtd avg shrs			 13,116    7,103   13,141</p>
<p>  NINE MONTHS ENDED		29-Dec-96 31-Dec-95  31-Dec-95</p>
<p>					   Actual     Actual  Pro Forma*</p>
<p> Net sales			   $233,554    $142,474  $321,101</p>
<p>Net income before loss on</p>
<p>  debt extinguishment	     $13,462	$8,758    $6,017</p>
<p>  Wgtd avg shrs			13,184	 7,048    13,085</p>
<p>  Net EPS before loss		 $1.02	 $1.24     $0.46</p>
<p>(In thousands, except per share and percentage data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Proforma on the basis that the acquisition of Lift-Tech International, Inc. and Spreckels Industries, Inc. (doing business as Yale International, Inc.) and the initial public offering of common stock took place as of the beginning of the periods presented.</p>
